description:
FOUND s499g while fixing #2442.  `pcl -Isub -e 'print "$INC[0]\n"'` prints `<root>/lib` where perl prints `sub`; `PERL5LIB=sub` the same.  The root comes from pl2cl's own `use lib dirname(abs_path($0))` and pcl's `-I $ROOT` (inc_dirs_for_transpile), which land in the emitted @INC and *p-core-inc-dirs*.  Resolution is right for every probed program (a module in the -I dir is still found; shims must win over perl's real Carp etc.), so this is ORDER only, plus the root entry.  DESIGN QUESTION before a fix: -I first would let a user dir shadow a PCL shim (perl's real List::Util in a local::lib PERL5LIB is the risk) -- measure, then decide; the root entry can probably simply be filtered out of the emitted list (check the runtime's child -I derivation does not need it: pl2cl finds Pl/ through its own use lib).

=== DONE (s499j) ===
@INC = -I (in order), PERL5LIB, PCL lib/, perl's own; the PCL root and tools/lib are gone (ONE derivation PCLPaths::program_inc: pl2cl preamble, Pl::Parser inc_paths, pcl seed; pcl stopped passing -I $ROOT). Nothing needed the root: pl2cl finds Pl/ through its own `use lib`, and the runtime's child -I derivation is the program's @INC. Must-win shims (`# pcl-shim: must-win` header marker, read by runtime %p-must-win-shim and Pl::Parser::must_win_shim): 12 XS shims + Test::More + Carp + Math::BigInt::Calc (the last two measured failing when perl's real copy is on PERL5LIB -- see #2491). Probes perl=tree (base differs): -I order, PERL5LIB order, root absent, require Pl::Parser dies, a user -I File::Spec::Functions wins, PERL5LIB with real List::Util+Carp runs. Guards Pl/t/pcl-dash-m-01.t rows 10-14 (inverse-verified except row 13, which the base also passes). Gate 269/9037 PASS; sweep TOTAL 18714 +0; EVERYDAY 102 -> 102.
